– Problems and solutions


Day 1 – Environment and local Git

 Problem 1: python -m venv inge_env failed

Cause: The inge_env folder already existed (first attempt succeeded, second blocked).
Solution: Delete the folder with Windows Explorer (because Remove-Item was locked), then run python -m venv inge_env again.

 Problem 2: Activation with .\inge_venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

Cause: Typo (inge_venv instead of inge_env).
Solution: Type the exact folder name: .\inge_env\Scripts\Activate.ps1.

 Problem 3: git confi user.email instead of git config

Cause: Typo.
Solution: Reread the command before pressing Enter.

 Problem 4: np._version_ instead of np.__version__

Cause: Confusion between a single underscore and two underscores.
Solution: np.__version__ (double underscore before and after).



Day 2 – SSH, GitHub and first push

 Problem 5: ssh-heygen instead of ssh-keygen

Cause: Typo (y instead of k).
Solution: Type ssh-keygen.

 Problem 6: Terminal blocked after pasting the entire history

Cause: Bad copy-paste (the entire history instead of the command).
Solution: Ctrl+C to cancel, or close the terminal (trash icon) and open a new one.

 Problem 7: Get-Content -/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub (hyphen instead of tilde)

Cause: -/.ssh instead of ~/.ssh.
Solution: Use ~/.ssh/... or the full path C:\Users\ADMIN\.ssh\....

 Problem 8: The SSH and GPG keys option not found

Cause: Simplified mobile interface.
Solution: Do the operation on the PC, or enable "Desktop version" in the mobile browser.

 Problem 9: git remote add origin git@github.com: Roland13-ai/... (space after )

Cause: Parasitic space after the colon.
Solution: Remove the space: git@github.com:Roland13-ai/....

 Problem 10: Could not resolve hostname github.com

Cause: Temporary network problem (DNS).
Solution: Check the connection with ping github.com. If the ping works, restart VS Code.

 Problem 11: Repository not found

Cause: The repository name on GitHub did not match the local name.
Solution: Rename the repository on GitHub (Settings → Repository name).

 Problem 12: Infinite scrolling of inge_env/ files

Cause: The .gitignore was not at the root. git add . indexed thousands of files.
Solution:

1. Ctrl+C to stop.
2. git rm -r --cached inge_env to remove the folder from the index.
3. Create .gitignore at the root with the appropriate content.
4. git add .gitignore then git commit.



Day 3 – circuits.py module

 Problem 13: TypeError: unsupported format string passed to function.__format__

Cause: Calling a function without parentheses. z_r contained the function itself, not its result.
Solution: Write z_r = impedance_resistance(r) with parentheses and parameters.

 Problem 14: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'circuits'

Cause: Python cannot find the module in the current folder.
Solution: Move to the folder containing circuits.py (cd 01_foundations\week1\day3) or use sys.path.insert.

 Problem 15: SyntaxWarning on a docstring

Cause: Code misplaced after the triple quotes """.
Solution: Check that the docstring is properly closed and that the code is on the next line.

