Day 6 – JupyterLab and Git conflict

 Problem 20: SyntaxError: unterminated string literal in Markdown

Cause: Unclosed quotes or missing $$.
Solution: Check that each $$ or $ is properly closed.

 Problem 21: circuits not recognized in the notebook

Cause: Incorrect path to day3.
Solution: Use Path.cwd().parent / "day3".

 Problem 22: git push rejected (rejected)

Cause: The remote repository has commits that you do not have locally.
Solution: git pull --rebase origin main then git push.
If a conflict appears, resolve it manually.

 Problem 23: Rebase conflict (course_of_the_day file)

Cause: The file was modified both locally and on GitHub.
Solution:

1. Open the file, remove the conflict markers (<<<<<<<, =======, >>>>>>>).
2. git add the file.
3. git rebase --continue.
4. If stuck in Vim: Esc then :wq then Enter.

 Problem 24: Stuck in Vim

Cause: git rebase --continue opened the Vim editor.
Solution: Esc, then :wq, then Enter.
If you want to cancel everything: git rebase --abort.

 Problem 25: detached HEAD

Cause: The rebase detached the branch head.
Solution: git checkout main to return to the main branch.

 Problem 26: Ultimate rescue plan

Cause: Situation too muddled.
Solution:

git rebase --abort          # Cancel the rebase
git checkout main           # Return to main
git pull origin main        # Retrieve the remote
git add .                   # Add the modifications
git commit -m "message"     # Commit
git push                    # Push
git push --force-with-lease # As a last resort

Command Usage
Ctrl+C Cancel a command in progress
git status View the current state of the repository
git rebase --abort Cancel a blocked rebase
git checkout main Return to the main branch
git rm -r --cached folder Remove a folder from the Git index
git push --force-with-lease Force the push (with caution)
ping github.com Test the connection to GitHub
Esc :wq Enter Quit Vim